{"id":"na36b419485","headline":"Fuel Tax Protest NZ Holds Forty Rallies Across the Country as Bishop Rules Out Cutting Excise and Willis Backs Away From January 2027 Increase","summary":"Fuel tax protesters held more than 40 rallies across New Zealand, calling for excise and road user charges to be halved. Minister Chris Bishop ruled out cuts, and Nicola Willis stepped back from a planned January 2027 increase.","why":"Fuel excise and road user charges affect transport costs and government revenue, and changes to them feed into inflation and household budgets.","category":"economy","event_type":"regulation","importance":1,"flag":null,"market_moving":false,"location":{"place":"Wellington","country":"New Zealand","lat":-41.29,"lon":174.78,"region":"oc"},"entities":[],"links":[],"source":{"name":"NEWS WIRE","url":"https://newswire.co.nz/2026/05/fuel-tax-protest-nz-forty-rallies-bishop-rules-out-cutting-excise/"},"sources":[{"name":"NEWS WIRE","url":"https://newswire.co.nz/2026/05/fuel-tax-protest-nz-forty-rallies-bishop-rules-out-cutting-excise/"}],"published_at":"2026-05-16T19:07:41Z","retrieved_at":"2026-11-17T15:49:20Z","official":false,"ai_summary":true,"content_hash":"281b0c40154c1643","impacts":[],"why_moved":null,"backfilled":true,"backfilled_at":"2026-11-17T15:49:20Z","backfill_provenance":{"version":"gdelt-backfill-v1","original_published_at":"2026-05-16T19:07:41Z","feed_url":"https://data.gdeltproject.org/gdeltv2/","discovered_via":"GDELT GKG 2.1","gdelt_seen":"2026-05-17T00:00:00Z","publisher_country_gdelt":"AS","description_from":"publisher page metadata"},"image":{"kind":"topic","file":"photos/parliament-government-building-51058.jpg","alt":"parliament government building (illustration)","credit":"PeterDargatz","license":"Pixabay Content License","license_url":"https://pixabay.com/service/license-summary/","source":"Pixabay","source_url":"https://pixabay.com/photos/architecture-building-landmark-51058/"}}